WEBVTT

00:00:13.080 --> 00:00:19.200
<i>C'mon, morning's here--time to be on our way</i>

00:00:19.200 --> 00:00:24.700
<i>Smiling faces, courage,</i>
<i>we're bustin' out: glory days!</i>

00:00:24.700 --> 00:00:29.830
<i>You ready or not? Ready or not, go!</i>
<i>No turning back: this trip is nonfiction</i>

00:00:29.830 --> 00:00:35.080
<i>You ready or not? Ready or not, go!</i>
<i>It's now or never, the real deal: Ready, and... action!</i>

00:00:35.080 --> 00:00:40.540
<i>Harsh winds that make us hesitate,</i>
<i>nights spent crying our eyes out</i>

00:00:40.540 --> 00:00:45.790
<i>They're not necessarily bad things (not bad)</i>

00:00:45.790 --> 00:00:51.500
<i>Just like the power in a spring:</i>
<i>the harder we're pushed</i>

00:00:51.500 --> 00:00:55.040
<i>The higher we can fly</i>

00:00:55.040 --> 00:01:05.580
<i>Face the far-off distance</i>
<i>and aim for the horizon: rising sun</i>

00:01:05.580 --> 00:01:10.870
<i>Holding our hands up to that morning sun</i>

00:01:10.870 --> 00:01:21.250
<i>Our shared feelings brought us together--</i>
<i>we're not alone anymore</i>

00:01:21.250 --> 00:01:27.450
<i>And so we're on this brilliant voyage</i>

00:01:27.450 --> 00:01:34.250
<i>Smiling faces, courage,</i>
<i>we're bustin' out: glory days!</i>

00:01:37.830 --> 00:01:41.620
Under the rule of Ei Sei,
the King who worked toward unification,

00:01:41.620 --> 00:01:45.410
the Kingdom of Chin launched
an invasion of the land of Gi.

00:01:45.410 --> 00:01:49.330
Their opponent: the legendary general Ren Pa.

00:01:49.330 --> 00:01:52.160
The young commanders stepped
onto a relentless battlefield,

00:01:52.160 --> 00:01:54.950
their sights set on a major victory.

00:01:55.000 --> 00:02:00.000
"General Caliber"

00:02:05.540 --> 00:02:06.750
These men--

00:02:13.080 --> 00:02:15.750
It was said that Gi's soldiers
were so deeply serious

00:02:15.750 --> 00:02:18.500
that they lacked raw explosive power.

00:02:18.500 --> 00:02:20.250
But with Ren Pa's appearance,

00:02:20.250 --> 00:02:22.580
they broke free of those bonds.

00:02:22.580 --> 00:02:24.700
Kill them! Killll!!

00:02:27.500 --> 00:02:28.790
Commander Heki!

00:02:28.790 --> 00:02:32.870
Sir, the sheer momentum of the Gi infantry--

00:02:32.870 --> 00:02:35.700
Stay calm... just stay calm...

00:02:35.700 --> 00:02:38.750
A commander needs to be
cool-headed at a time like this...

00:02:42.160 --> 00:02:45.040
The clifftops are still under our control...

00:02:49.250 --> 00:02:53.250
The Chin army still has all
the advantages of this terrain!

00:02:53.250 --> 00:02:55.370
The only part of the clifftops we've lost

00:02:55.370 --> 00:02:59.250
is right where Ren Pa appeared.

00:02:59.250 --> 00:03:00.620
I've got it!

00:03:00.620 --> 00:03:03.410
Given how quickly Ren Pa
came here from their main camp,

00:03:03.410 --> 00:03:07.120
and how we didn't see him coming at all...

00:03:08.500 --> 00:03:12.950
I'd generously estimate his troops
at a thousand men!

00:03:12.950 --> 00:03:15.870
Taking into account the casualties thus far,

00:03:15.870 --> 00:03:21.500
I'd say there are maybe eight thousand
Gi troops to Chin's ten.

00:03:21.500 --> 00:03:24.370
Almost no difference at all on numbers alone.

00:03:24.370 --> 00:03:27.870
Ren Pa's appearance may have
given their morale a boost,

00:03:27.870 --> 00:03:31.700
but we still have the absolute
advantage in these straits!

00:03:31.700 --> 00:03:34.450
Defeating Ren Pa
all comes down to how we fight!

00:03:37.540 --> 00:03:40.450
Kyou En is fleeing to the other side!

00:03:40.450 --> 00:03:41.750
Let him go.

00:03:42.700 --> 00:03:45.250
Our central army is a mess.

00:03:45.250 --> 00:03:47.830
Get the commanders out there
to rebuild our formations.

00:03:47.830 --> 00:03:48.830
Sir!

00:03:50.790 --> 00:03:54.750
So they're regrouping first, eh?

00:03:56.620 --> 00:04:01.080
And then what will you do, Ou Sen?

00:04:01.080 --> 00:04:06.950
Ren Pa was interested in
Ou Sen's actions from here on out.

00:04:06.950 --> 00:04:09.160
The armies were evenly matched in numbers.

00:04:09.160 --> 00:04:12.450
The Chin army had the
benefit of the ideal terrain,

00:04:12.450 --> 00:04:14.870
while the Gi army was riding high
on a wave of morale.

00:04:14.870 --> 00:04:17.120
A strategist couldn't ask for better ingredients

00:04:17.120 --> 00:04:19.620
with which to show his skills.

00:04:21.330 --> 00:04:23.000
All squads regrouped!

00:04:24.450 --> 00:04:27.910
Just watch that they don't
chip away at our main units.

00:04:27.910 --> 00:04:29.580
Understood, sir.

00:04:29.580 --> 00:04:32.830
Considered by Ou Ki to be
on a par with Chin's six great generals,

00:04:32.830 --> 00:04:36.500
it remained to be seen
what dish Ou Sen would cook up.

00:04:36.500 --> 00:04:39.450
Ren Pa was using this battle as a yardstick

00:04:39.450 --> 00:04:42.200
to measure Ou Sen's military worth.

00:04:43.290 --> 00:04:44.870
However,

00:04:44.870 --> 00:04:49.250
Ou Sen would betray Ren Pa's
expectations most splendidly.

00:04:49.250 --> 00:04:50.290
All right--

00:04:51.750 --> 00:04:53.660
All troops, retreat.

00:04:59.830 --> 00:05:01.160
We're pulling out?

00:05:01.160 --> 00:05:03.080
With such a perfect opportunity? Why?

00:05:03.080 --> 00:05:06.160
I don't know!
We're bringing up the rear--look sharp!

00:05:13.250 --> 00:05:14.790
Sorry, Ren Pa--

00:05:18.540 --> 00:05:22.580
I'm only interested in battles
I'm guaranteed to win.

00:05:25.700 --> 00:05:27.620
I see...

00:05:27.620 --> 00:05:30.330
Kill 'em! Don't let 'em get away!

00:05:30.330 --> 00:05:31.790
Heki, sir, move further ahead!

00:05:31.790 --> 00:05:34.330
No! We can't abandon the infantry!

00:05:34.330 --> 00:05:35.700
Calvary, provide backup!

00:05:35.700 --> 00:05:38.620
That's too reckless! Behind us there's--

00:05:46.040 --> 00:05:48.000
I do not understand.

00:05:48.000 --> 00:05:51.830
Why are you so happy to have been thwarted so?

00:05:51.830 --> 00:05:53.870
I'm happy, am I?

00:05:53.870 --> 00:05:55.160
You seem so.

00:05:56.500 --> 00:05:58.450
Then perhaps I am!

00:05:58.450 --> 00:06:03.160
Who among Chin's six great generals
have you fought, Kyou En?

00:06:03.160 --> 00:06:05.080
Of the six great generals?

00:06:06.620 --> 00:06:08.250
Haku Ki,

00:06:08.250 --> 00:06:09.950
Ou Kotsu,

00:06:09.950 --> 00:06:11.450
Ou Ki,

00:06:11.450 --> 00:06:14.040
and Kyou: these four.

00:06:14.040 --> 00:06:16.660
And who was the most intense?

00:06:16.660 --> 00:06:21.290
Intense? For me, that was Kyou.

00:06:21.290 --> 00:06:24.750
Our mutual emphasis on offense
always meant countless casualties

00:06:24.750 --> 00:06:26.160
on both sides.

00:06:27.790 --> 00:06:31.750
Kyou's attacks always
<i>were</i> particularly heinous...

00:06:31.750 --> 00:06:34.910
Then who was the hardest to handle?

00:06:36.330 --> 00:06:39.120
Haku Ki, leader of the six great generals.

00:06:39.120 --> 00:06:42.410
I thought so. He was my toughest, too.

00:06:42.410 --> 00:06:45.750
Haku Ki, now, he was no risk-taker.

00:06:45.750 --> 00:06:48.370
No matter how tasty
the bait dangled before him,

00:06:48.370 --> 00:06:50.120
he never rose to take it.

00:06:50.120 --> 00:06:52.250
The more muscular my approach became,

00:06:52.250 --> 00:06:56.290
the more slow and relaxed his response.

00:06:56.290 --> 00:07:00.160
He always had a read on
his opponent's state of mind.

00:07:00.160 --> 00:07:04.450
Infuriated, I would chase Haku Ki too far,
only to have him retaliate.

00:07:04.450 --> 00:07:07.160
That was our routine.

00:07:09.290 --> 00:07:11.500
Why mention this now?

00:07:12.540 --> 00:07:15.000
It's just that, somehow,

00:07:15.000 --> 00:07:17.870
watching Ou Sen as he sauntered away

00:07:17.870 --> 00:07:20.700
reminded me of Haku Ki.

00:07:22.200 --> 00:07:24.160
Then Ou Sen is equal to Haku Ki?

00:07:25.830 --> 00:07:28.250
I wouldn't go <i>that</i> far.

00:07:28.250 --> 00:07:33.200
But their fighting styles
have several points in common.

00:07:33.200 --> 00:07:36.290
And similar fighting styles

00:07:36.290 --> 00:07:40.950
may indicate they share
a similar view of the world.

00:07:40.950 --> 00:07:45.410
True, his scheme to appear
in the straits was superb.

00:07:45.410 --> 00:07:47.370
But based on that alone?

00:07:47.370 --> 00:07:51.620
In any case, Haku Ki was
a monster through and through--

00:07:51.620 --> 00:07:54.200
Alert! Alert!

00:07:54.200 --> 00:07:57.580
Up ahead! It's the enemy's--the enemy's--

00:07:57.580 --> 00:07:59.580
Just please, hurry onward!

00:08:03.250 --> 00:08:09.250
Field warfare, castle onslaughts,
sieges--Haku Ki did it all.

00:08:09.250 --> 00:08:14.080
How many times had I chased
after his army, just like this?

00:08:14.080 --> 00:08:17.910
Wherever he ran to would
have something waiting there

00:08:17.910 --> 00:08:20.370
to stop me in my tracks.

00:08:20.370 --> 00:08:24.660
For example, you'd be here in the mountains,
and before you know it...

00:08:31.160 --> 00:08:34.410
...he'd have constructed a giant castle!

00:08:35.750 --> 00:08:37.160
Well played...

00:08:37.160 --> 00:08:39.540
Very few commanders can pull off
building a fortification

00:08:39.540 --> 00:08:41.700
in the middle of a campaign.

00:08:41.700 --> 00:08:44.660
This is enough to know the extent of his skill.

00:08:44.660 --> 00:08:48.120
Could he have built this
in expectation of my arrival...?

00:08:50.370 --> 00:08:52.580
What a surprise!

00:08:52.580 --> 00:08:54.700
To think a man like you

00:08:54.700 --> 00:08:58.790
was still hiding in the shadows
of the six great generals,

00:08:58.790 --> 00:09:00.160
Ou Sen!

00:09:01.410 --> 00:09:03.370
A natural stronghold...

00:09:03.370 --> 00:09:07.830
Ou Sen has seen more terrain
in this battle than anyone else,

00:09:07.830 --> 00:09:12.580
but to find something like this--
<i>and</i> those straits?

00:09:12.580 --> 00:09:15.040
We are not prepared to attack such a fortress,

00:09:15.040 --> 00:09:18.660
and to strike unprepared
would mean many casualties.

00:09:18.660 --> 00:09:21.370
Killing him would be next to impossible.

00:09:23.620 --> 00:09:28.450
What is this?! Ou Sen, you bastard!

00:09:32.200 --> 00:09:33.370
Kyou En!

00:09:33.370 --> 00:09:34.290
My lord?

00:09:34.290 --> 00:09:38.580
Prepare a camp. We'll surround this fortress!

00:09:38.580 --> 00:09:39.580
Yes, sir!

00:09:41.310 --> 00:09:44.930
"Heki"

00:09:52.040 --> 00:09:54.080
What's with them?

00:09:54.080 --> 00:09:55.620
That's the Hi Shin Unit.

00:09:55.620 --> 00:09:59.330
Seems their commander still hasn't come back.

00:09:59.330 --> 00:10:02.500
Enemy attacks during the battle
between the central armies

00:10:02.500 --> 00:10:06.120
had plunged the Chin army's
formations into disorder.

00:10:06.120 --> 00:10:09.080
The battle was so chaotic that
the squads that had gone off alone

00:10:09.080 --> 00:10:12.290
still had not returned
to their original positions.

00:10:12.290 --> 00:10:14.660
Please rest, Lieutenant.

00:10:20.120 --> 00:10:21.620
L-Look!

00:10:28.750 --> 00:10:30.250
S-Shin!

00:10:30.250 --> 00:10:31.370
It's Shin!

00:10:31.370 --> 00:10:32.750
--Shin's back!
--Commander!

00:10:32.750 --> 00:10:34.870
--Thank goodness!
--Shin!

00:10:34.870 --> 00:10:36.160
It's Shin!

00:10:41.200 --> 00:10:42.620
Mou Ten, sir,

00:10:42.620 --> 00:10:46.200
Generals Do Mon and Ei Bi await.

00:10:46.200 --> 00:10:47.660
Yeah, I know.

00:10:55.870 --> 00:10:58.370
We may still have someone on our tail!

00:10:58.370 --> 00:11:00.160
We can't rest!

00:11:00.160 --> 00:11:02.200
Stay alert and keep going!

00:11:03.370 --> 00:11:09.000
What <i>are</i> you, General Ou Sen?
What are you thinking?

00:11:09.000 --> 00:11:14.080
Using us as a decoy,
sacrificing all those soldiers--

00:11:14.080 --> 00:11:16.040
Only to run?

00:11:17.290 --> 00:11:21.250
Never mind Kyou En.
You're the one I don't understand.

00:11:22.870 --> 00:11:26.750
Rare is the commander
with fortress-building capabilities.

00:11:26.750 --> 00:11:30.700
Of the six great generals,
only Haku Ki could do so...

00:11:30.700 --> 00:11:33.660
I had my share of trouble
with Haku Ki's defenses;

00:11:33.660 --> 00:11:37.290
this fine building stands up to any of his.

00:11:37.290 --> 00:11:40.870
Indeed, the depth of his tactics
and his distinctiveness

00:11:40.870 --> 00:11:43.330
may well match those of Haku Ki...

00:11:44.580 --> 00:11:50.120
But this is where you differ greatly,
Ou Sen...

00:11:50.120 --> 00:11:52.790
You are a lieutenant,

00:11:52.790 --> 00:11:59.160
and in this battle, you saw yourself
as the Chin army's best and brightest.

00:11:59.160 --> 00:12:03.200
Your behavior made that clear.

00:12:03.200 --> 00:12:05.000
Indeed.

00:12:05.000 --> 00:12:08.750
It may be difficult for us to strike
Ou Sen in that fortress,

00:12:08.750 --> 00:12:13.910
but on the other hand,
we have him trapped here.

00:12:13.910 --> 00:12:18.000
If the Chin army's main power
is in its left and right flanks,

00:12:18.000 --> 00:12:19.410
this will come as a terrific blow.

00:12:20.790 --> 00:12:22.700
Plus, this erases half the means

00:12:22.700 --> 00:12:25.750
the Chin army had to cope
with a worst-case scenario.

00:12:26.870 --> 00:12:29.200
Surely he must have realized that!

00:12:30.540 --> 00:12:36.620
My land has need of a
war-strong man such as yourself.

00:12:37.950 --> 00:12:43.120
It would seem Ou Sen is
lacking something as a commander.

00:12:43.120 --> 00:12:45.410
Greatly lacking!

00:12:45.410 --> 00:12:48.200
The man is twisted indeed.

00:12:48.200 --> 00:12:52.000
Ou Sen, I know why you never
let the sun shine on you until today--

00:12:52.000 --> 00:12:56.040
going back to the days of King Sho.

00:12:56.040 --> 00:13:00.830
A commander who puts
himself first cannot be trusted.

00:13:00.830 --> 00:13:06.580
No matter how skilled you are in battle,
none will see you as a hero.

00:13:06.580 --> 00:13:10.580
You stand on a different path than we do.

00:13:13.120 --> 00:13:16.750
I won't go so far as to discount you completely,

00:13:16.750 --> 00:13:19.200
but I've lost interest.

00:13:19.200 --> 00:13:22.410
I leave this place to you, Kyou En.

00:13:22.410 --> 00:13:27.160
Ou Sen has essentially removed
himself from the battlefield.

00:13:27.160 --> 00:13:29.950
He won't be making any moves for a while.

00:13:29.950 --> 00:13:31.410
And you, my lord?

00:13:31.410 --> 00:13:35.830
I'm going back to basics:
War is about killing the general.

00:13:35.830 --> 00:13:38.250
Perhaps it's time I give that
miserable old acquaintance of mine

00:13:38.250 --> 00:13:40.410
a proper sendoff...

00:13:41.790 --> 00:13:45.790
I'll have this war over tomorrow, Kyou En!

00:13:45.790 --> 00:13:46.790
Yes, sir!

00:13:50.660 --> 00:13:54.660
So Do Mon and Ei Bi
have given you a piece of their minds.

00:13:54.660 --> 00:13:57.620
Yes--and one slap apiece.

00:13:59.790 --> 00:14:02.500
I'm glad it ended there!

00:14:02.500 --> 00:14:05.200
What is it you needed, General, sir?

00:14:05.200 --> 00:14:10.620
Enough of that. Here we're
just a grandpa and his grandson.

00:14:10.620 --> 00:14:12.370
Come here, Tian.

00:14:12.370 --> 00:14:15.950
What's wrong, Grandpa? You're acting different.

00:14:15.950 --> 00:14:17.790
I don't like it.

00:14:17.790 --> 00:14:20.290
Don't say that, Tian.

00:14:20.290 --> 00:14:25.000
Strangely, there are some things
you come to understand at my age...

00:14:25.000 --> 00:14:28.950
like when a desperate battle is approaching.

00:14:28.950 --> 00:14:31.160
See? That's not like you at all.

00:14:31.160 --> 00:14:34.660
Staying calm and reasonable
in battle is the Haku Rou way!

00:14:36.620 --> 00:14:41.540
Usually, yes. But this time...

00:14:41.540 --> 00:14:44.120
...this time I won't back down.

00:14:54.370 --> 00:14:56.580
Shin, you--those wounds!

00:14:56.580 --> 00:14:58.000
I-I see bone...

00:14:59.000 --> 00:15:00.750
They do look a little deep, huh...

00:15:05.410 --> 00:15:08.160
Wait here. I'll bring medicine.

00:15:08.160 --> 00:15:11.870
All you dirty gawkers, get out!
You'll make his wounds worse.

00:15:11.870 --> 00:15:13.580
Seriously?

00:15:13.580 --> 00:15:16.410
Get away from him! Go on, everyone--get out!

00:15:38.330 --> 00:15:41.660
So it's left its mark,

00:15:41.660 --> 00:15:43.330
that wound...

00:15:49.040 --> 00:15:50.580
Does your wound still hurt?

00:15:50.580 --> 00:15:55.790
Huh? Oh... n-no, the pain's all gone!

00:15:55.790 --> 00:15:56.790
But...?

00:16:07.120 --> 00:16:08.540
Whoa! Whoa whoa whoa!

00:16:08.540 --> 00:16:10.290
Look, Kou.

00:16:12.250 --> 00:16:15.790
I got these during my brother's uprising.

00:16:15.790 --> 00:16:16.660
Are they ugly?

00:16:16.660 --> 00:16:19.370
A-Absolutely not! N-Not at all!

00:16:19.370 --> 00:16:20.080
That's a lie.

00:16:20.080 --> 00:16:22.700
It's not! I swear!

00:16:22.700 --> 00:16:25.250
They're proof that Your Highness survived--

00:16:25.250 --> 00:16:27.750
so I don't find them ugly in the slightest!

00:16:27.750 --> 00:16:32.790
Then I don't find your wound ugly, either.

00:16:34.290 --> 00:16:35.500
Do you believe me?

00:16:39.750 --> 00:16:43.500
Y-Yes... I do.

00:16:43.500 --> 00:16:45.040
I do believe you...

00:16:53.000 --> 00:16:54.410
Buck up.

00:16:55.500 --> 00:16:57.450
What <i>is</i> that?!

00:16:57.450 --> 00:17:03.410
A medicine from my village,
compounded from special herbs.

00:17:03.410 --> 00:17:06.410
I'd been gathering them the
whole time we've been marching,

00:17:06.410 --> 00:17:09.120
but this shellful is all it made.

00:17:09.120 --> 00:17:12.370
Use that precious stuff on yourself,
then, ya dummy!

00:17:12.370 --> 00:17:15.870
So Sui told me how you were
bitin' off more than you can chew!

00:17:15.870 --> 00:17:18.330
I don't screw up like you do.

00:17:20.500 --> 00:17:22.000
Thanks.

00:17:26.120 --> 00:17:28.000
Wh-What?

00:17:29.290 --> 00:17:32.160
That Rin Ko guy--

00:17:32.160 --> 00:17:34.790
I take it he was strong?

00:17:34.790 --> 00:17:37.540
"Strong" doesn't even begin to cover it.

00:17:37.540 --> 00:17:41.040
I mean, he wasn't a monster
like Hou Ken, but then again,

00:17:41.040 --> 00:17:43.790
you can't go comparing those two.

00:17:43.790 --> 00:17:47.120
He had the strength of a man
who'd fought many battles,

00:17:47.120 --> 00:17:51.700
who'd faced death and overcome
his own limits time and time again...

00:17:51.700 --> 00:17:54.700
And me, too, I--

00:17:54.700 --> 00:17:58.450
Well, I don't really know how to put this...

00:17:58.450 --> 00:18:03.160
but I feel like I've overcome
one of my own limits, too.

00:18:06.120 --> 00:18:09.660
I see. So that's what it is.

00:18:09.660 --> 00:18:15.370
Even all beat-up like this,
his presence is bigger than before.

00:18:16.910 --> 00:18:20.250
Guess it's kinda weird for
the loser to be sayin' that, huh.

00:18:21.540 --> 00:18:26.330
But look, all these people were dyin'
and I went and screwed up.

00:18:26.330 --> 00:18:28.910
And I'm gonna settle that once and for all!

00:18:28.910 --> 00:18:32.370
Next time for sure--
I'll kill 'im by my own hand!

00:18:33.950 --> 00:18:37.290
Then get some sleep and recover.

00:18:37.290 --> 00:18:40.330
You're not fighting anyone
till that fever's gone.

00:18:40.330 --> 00:18:44.200
With your medicine,
I'll be my old self in the morning!

00:18:44.200 --> 00:18:46.040
You will not.

00:18:46.040 --> 00:18:48.410
Things ain't that convenient, eh?

00:18:55.700 --> 00:18:58.330
What the hell? You sleepin' here?

00:18:58.330 --> 00:19:03.540
That medicine is strong.
Your body might reject it.

00:19:03.540 --> 00:19:05.870
I'll keep an eye on you for a while.

00:19:05.870 --> 00:19:08.540
But really, you want to be with me.

00:19:08.540 --> 00:19:09.950
Nevermind.

00:19:09.950 --> 00:19:12.830
If your condition worsens, feel free to die.

00:19:12.830 --> 00:19:14.450
I was kidding! Kidding!

00:19:25.660 --> 00:19:30.370
Once this war's over,
we won't be able to talk like this.

00:19:30.370 --> 00:19:33.330
Hate to say this, but I'll miss it.

00:19:33.330 --> 00:19:36.160
Don't worry about anything past tomorrow.

00:19:36.160 --> 00:19:39.910
This war won't end that easily.

00:19:39.910 --> 00:19:41.790
Yeah...

00:19:41.790 --> 00:19:42.950
...you're right.

00:20:01.290 --> 00:20:02.620
Ow ow ow...

00:20:04.200 --> 00:20:07.120
Now that I look around,
it's like everyone's injured.

00:20:07.120 --> 00:20:09.080
Well, of course.

00:20:09.080 --> 00:20:10.450
How many days has it been?

00:20:11.700 --> 00:20:14.540
I guess it makes sense,
having so many injured soldiers.

00:20:14.540 --> 00:20:17.790
But Shin's hurt worst of all.

00:20:17.790 --> 00:20:19.620
With a fever on top of those cuts,

00:20:19.620 --> 00:20:21.700
he'll be flat on his back for two, three--

00:20:24.580 --> 00:20:25.870
Hey! Who did that?!

00:20:25.870 --> 00:20:28.080
It's too early... for...

00:20:28.080 --> 00:20:29.870
Yo, Bi Hei!

00:20:32.290 --> 00:20:33.540
S-Shin?!

00:20:33.540 --> 00:20:35.910
A-Are you... are you okay?

00:20:35.910 --> 00:20:37.790
Fine! See?

00:20:37.790 --> 00:20:38.870
And...

00:20:38.870 --> 00:20:41.000
...see?

00:20:41.000 --> 00:20:41.870
Whoa!

00:20:41.870 --> 00:20:43.290
That's our commander!

00:20:43.290 --> 00:20:44.410
Amazing!

00:20:44.410 --> 00:20:46.910
--That went down to the <i>bone</i> !
--Yep, that's Commander Shin, all right!

00:20:46.910 --> 00:20:49.290
You sure did heal up quick, Shin.

00:20:49.290 --> 00:20:52.370
Honestly, I thought your right hand was a goner.

00:20:52.370 --> 00:20:54.040
It was Kyou Kai.

00:20:54.040 --> 00:20:56.620
Gave me some great medicine
that was in awful short supply.

00:20:56.620 --> 00:20:58.870
It wasn't just the medicine.

00:20:58.870 --> 00:21:00.250
Kyou Kai?

00:21:00.250 --> 00:21:02.540
It was half thanks to the medicine

00:21:02.540 --> 00:21:06.660
and half thanks to your own
crazy power of recovery.

00:21:17.040 --> 00:21:18.160
Kyou Kai...

00:21:21.910 --> 00:21:23.000
Kyou Kai!

00:21:26.540 --> 00:21:29.160
Today's the day we crush the Gi army!

00:21:33.120 --> 00:21:36.540
All right! Time to start
gettin' ready for another charge!

00:21:36.540 --> 00:21:38.330
We're gonna hit 'em hard!

00:21:45.500 --> 00:21:48.500
<i>They</i> sure are starting the day off right!

00:21:50.120 --> 00:21:53.910
This was the sixth day
in the battle on the Rui Plains.

00:21:53.910 --> 00:21:56.830
It had been about two and
a half months since the Chin army

00:21:56.830 --> 00:22:00.200
had embarked on the Sanyou Offensive.

00:22:00.200 --> 00:22:03.370
Though they had taken 16 fortified cities,

00:22:03.370 --> 00:22:07.370
their goal was still to secure Sanyou,

00:22:07.370 --> 00:22:10.080
the militarily vital stronghold beyond them all.

00:22:10.080 --> 00:22:11.910
Unless the Chin army could destroy the Gi army,

00:22:11.910 --> 00:22:14.120
which had mobilized to protect Sanyou,

00:22:14.120 --> 00:22:18.330
their entire offensive would end in failure.

00:22:18.330 --> 00:22:20.160
Defending Gi,

00:22:20.160 --> 00:22:23.120
attacking Chin, and

00:22:23.120 --> 00:22:26.830
the strong foes from other lands
who watched them:

00:22:26.830 --> 00:22:28.620
the myriad great thoughts and expectations

00:22:28.620 --> 00:22:30.580
of the entire Middle Kingdom

00:22:30.580 --> 00:22:33.410
were focused solely on Sanyou.

00:22:53.450 --> 00:22:54.450
Shin?

00:22:56.040 --> 00:22:58.000
Guess they can't see me, huh?

00:22:59.330 --> 00:23:02.160
And there, the men who risked their lives

00:23:02.160 --> 00:23:04.040
in the battle at its very center,

00:23:04.040 --> 00:23:06.370
came to a strange realization:

00:23:08.870 --> 00:23:12.000
Yes, of course...

00:23:12.000 --> 00:23:15.080
The curtain was now rising

00:23:15.080 --> 00:23:18.540
on the final day of the
Great Sanyou Offensive!

00:23:22.830 --> 00:23:31.370
<i>I'm dreaming of you, just like back then</i>

00:23:31.370 --> 00:23:39.830
<i>Trusting, unafraid of anything</i>

00:23:39.830 --> 00:23:48.080
<i>Your words that I always remember</i>

00:23:48.080 --> 00:23:56.540
<i>Are getting fainter,</i>
<i>mixed up, about to disappear</i>

00:23:56.540 --> 00:24:01.500
<i>I go crazy trying to make them out</i>

00:24:01.500 --> 00:24:05.830
<i>Barefoot still, I'd lost my way</i>

00:24:05.830 --> 00:24:10.080
<i>It's okay to stop</i>

00:24:10.080 --> 00:24:14.250
<i>But even if I go after you,</i>
<i>if I hold out my hand</i>

00:24:14.250 --> 00:24:17.500
<i>Don't respond just yet</i>

00:24:17.500 --> 00:24:22.700
<i>But until I forget, don't change</i>

00:24:22.700 --> 00:24:26.870
<i>I ask this of you, and yet</i>

00:24:26.870 --> 00:24:34.200
<i>Like a long-awaited morning, it's starting again</i>

00:24:34.200 --> 00:24:37.700
<i>And I still remember</i>

00:24:52.000 --> 00:24:58.010
"Next Episode Preview"

00:25:02.000 --> 00:25:07.020
"Showdown"
